<title>EGYPT: Egypt pound rates inch higher in liquid market.</title>
<headline>Egypt pound rates inch higher in liquid market.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Overnight interbank rates on the Egyptian pound rose slightly on Monday to between 7-1/2 and 8 percent in a flush private-sector market from seven and 7-1/2 percent on Sunday, bankers said.</p>
<p>Many bankers said they avoided overnight deals because of the excessive liquidity which flowed into the market from last week and said they made one-week trades at rates ranging between 7-1/8 and 8-1/2 percent. One-week rates were 7-3/16 and 8-3/4 percent on Sunday.</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +202 578 3290/1</p>
